{
  "version": "0.5.2",
  "status": "review",
  "notes": [
    "Curated unit mappings promoted from decisions in interactive review.",
    "These entries are treated as authoritative for JSON->RDF conversion.",
    "IRIs verified against EMMO 1.0.2, domain-battery 0.21.0, domain-electrochemistry 0.39.0 and domain-chemical-substance 0.15.0. From domain-electrochemistry 0.38.0 the closure imports EMMO's siacceptedunits module, so the hour- and litre-based units (AmpereHour, MilliAmpereHour, Watthour, KiloWatthour, MolePerLitre, WattHourPerKilogram, WattHourPerLitre, MilliLitre) are declared in it under the same EMMO IRIs this map already used.",
    "All candidates with confidence 1.0 promoted. MANUAL_UNIT_TYPES entries consolidated here.",
    "Wh/kg and Wh/L use EMMO IRIs (confirmed present). W/kg uses QUDT (not in EMMO core).",
    "Wh and kWh: EMMO spells the local names Watthour / KiloWatthour (lower-case h) while the prefLabels read WattHour / KiloWattHour; the IRIs follow EMMO, the labels follow the prefLabel.",
    "0.5.0: added 1, mS/cm, m2/g, g/mol, mol/kg, nm, mPa.s, mg, Hz, A/Ah, kg/m3, cm3, cm2; IRIs verified against the bundled domain-battery context. ASCII aliases (um, mg/cm^2, mOhm, ...) are normalised in code, not listed here.",
    "0.5.1: added mA/cm2, A/cm2 and A/m2 for current densities in test methods (coin-cell protocols state their currents per area). IRIs checked in EMMO 1.0.2 disciplines/units/noncoherentsiunits.ttl (MilliAmperePerSquareCentiMetre, AmperePerSquareCentiMetre) and coherentsiunits.ttl (AmperePerSquareMetre), all subclasses of ElectricCurrentDensityUnit, and present in the bundled domain-battery context.",
    "0.5.2: added the SI units BPX states its parameters in: m2, m3, mol/m3, m2/s, J/mol, V/K, S/m, 1/m, mol.m-2.s-1, J/(kg.K), W/(m.K) and W/(m2.K). IRIs checked in EMMO 1.0.2 disciplines/units/coherentsiunits.ttl (SquareMetre, CubicMetre, MolePerCubicMetre, SquareMetrePerSecond, JoulePerMole, VoltPerKelvin, SiemensPerMetre, PerMetre, MolePerSquareMetrePerSecond, JoulePerKilogramKelvin, WattPerMetreKelvin, WattPerSquareMetreKelvin), all present in the bundled domain-battery context."
  ],
